-- title:
--   Caccetta–Häggkvist for $r = 2$
-- statement:
--   **The rung $r=2$ of the Caccetta–Häggkvist conjecture** (Caccetta and Häggkvist, 1978). Every loopless digraph on $n\ge 1$ vertices in which every vertex has out-degree at least $2$ contains a directed cycle of length at most $\lceil n/2\rceil$:
--
--   $$\delta^+(D)\ge 2 \implies \text{girth}(D)\le\lceil n/2\rceil .$$
-- source:
--   L. Caccetta, R. Häggkvist, On minimal digraphs with given girth, Proc. 9th Southeastern Conf. (1978), Congr. Numer. 21, 181–187, Theorem for out-degree 2

